APPLESIDE -- AN APPLESOFT EDITOR
AND A COMPILER FOR WHAT YOU WRITE.

THE EDITOR
  RETURN         SUPPLIES THE NEXT LINE
                 NUMBER
  ?              TYPES PRINT
  CTRL-R         SAVE, DROP INTO BASIC,
                 AND RUN IT
  OA-R           RENUMBER BY TEN.  EVERY
                 GOTO, GOSUB, THEN AND
                 RUN FOLLOWS ITS LINE.
  OA-K           CHECK EVERY GOTO TARGET
                 EXISTS
  OA-L           GO TO A LINE BY NUMBER
  OA-F OA-G      FIND, AND FIND AGAIN
  OA-C OA-X OA-V COPY, CUT AND PASTE
  OA-/           HINT ROW: OFF, NORMAL,
                 INVERSE
  OA-?           KEYBOARD HELP
  CTRL-Y         DELETE TO END OF LINE
  OA-S OA-O      SAVE AND OPEN
  OA-Q           QUIT STRAIGHT TO BASIC

  OA-LEFT/RIGHT  A WORD AT A TIME
  OA-UP/DOWN     A PAGE AT A TIME

  KEYWORDS DRAW INVERSE AS YOU TYPE.
  LONG LINES SCROLL SIDEWAYS; THE LINE
  NUMBER STAYS PINNED AT THE LEFT.

RUNNING WHAT YOU WRITE
  CTRL-R SAVES, LEAVES, AND RUNS IT.
  COME BACK WITH -ASIDE.SYSTEM AND YOUR
  PROGRAM IS LOADED AGAIN ALREADY.

COMPILING IT
  FROM THE ] PROMPT:

    -ASIDECC.SYSTEM
    COMPILE WHICH FILE? YOURNAME

  IT WRITES CYOURNAME AND PUTS YOU BACK
  AT THE ].  THEN:

    BRUN CYOURNAME

  FIVE TO TWELVE TIMES QUICKER, AND THE
  SAME ANSWERS.

  IT COMPILES LET, GOTO, GOSUB, RETURN,
  POP, IF/THEN, FOR AND NEXT WITH STEP,
  ON..GOTO, ON..GOSUB, DATA, READ,
  RESTORE, INPUT, GET, DEF FN, POKE,
  CALL, PRINT WITH ; AND , AND TAB(
  AND SPC(, REM, END, STOP, CLEAR AND
  RUN.

  THE SCREEN: HOME, HTAB, VTAB, TEXT,
  INVERSE, NORMAL, FLASH, SPEED=, PR#
  AND LOMEM:.

  GRAPHICS: GR, COLOR=, PLOT, HLIN AND
  VLIN, AND HGR, HGR2, HCOLOR= AND
  HPLOT, INCLUDING HPLOT TO.

  VARIABLES: REAL AND INTEGER, ARRAYS
  OF ONE TO THREE DIMENSIONS, STRING
  ARRAYS, AND DIM WITH A SIZE WORKED
  OUT WHILE IT RUNS.

  STRINGS: A$ = B$ + C$, COMPARING
  THEM, AND LEN, LEFT$, RIGHT$, MID$,
  ASC, CHR$, STR$ AND VAL.  THEY LIVE
  IN A HEAP WITH A GARBAGE COLLECTOR,
  SO BUILDING THEM IN A LOOP RUNS AS
  FAR AS APPLESOFT WOULD.

  AND THE ELEVEN NUMERIC FUNCTIONS,
  WITH PEEK, FRE, POS, PDL AND SCRN(.

  NOT YET: ONERR, INTEGER ARRAYS, THE
  SHAPE TABLE STATEMENTS, HIMEM:, IN#,
  WAIT, TRACE AND USR.  IT NAMES THE
  LINE AND STOPS RATHER THAN COMPILING
  THEM WRONGLY:

    STOPPED IN 30: STATEMENT NOT YET

A SAMPLE TO TRY
  MANDELBROT IS ON THIS DISK.  OPEN IT
  IN THE EDITOR WITH OA-O TO SEE WHAT
  A PROGRAM LOOKS LIKE IN IT, OR RUN
  IT FROM THE ] PROMPT:

    RUN MANDELBROT

  IT PLOTS 1600 POINTS AND TAKES A
  WHILE.  THEN COMPILE IT AND:

    BRUN CMANDELBROT

  SAME PICTURE.  THAT IS THE WHOLE
  ARGUMENT FOR THE COMPILER, IN ONE
  PROGRAM YOU CAN READ IN A MINUTE.

WHAT IS WORTH REPORTING
  ANYTHING THAT DROPS A CHARACTER WHILE
  YOU TYPE.  THE EMULATOR CANNOT SHOW
  THAT AND A REAL APPLE CAN.

  ANYTHING THAT HIGHLIGHTS A WORD THAT
  IS NOT A KEYWORD, OR MISSES ONE THAT
  IS -- ESPECIALLY IN A LONG LINE THAT
  HAS SCROLLED.

  ANY RENUMBER THAT MOVES A GOTO TO THE
  WRONG PLACE.  THERE IS NO UNDO, SO IF
  ONE GOES WRONG, DO NOT SAVE.

  ANY PROGRAM THAT SAVES AND THEN WILL
  NOT RUN, OR COMES BACK DIFFERENT.

  ANY COMPILED PROGRAM THAT PRINTS
  SOMETHING DIFFERENT FROM WHAT RUN
  PRINTS.  THAT ONE IS THE MOST USEFUL
  OF ALL.

  NEEDS AN ENHANCED //E WITH 128K.
